Ryan Ficklin, Madeline Park

See report pdf for information on contribution, system design, etc. 

Running the program should be performed similar to the video provided
specification. Multiple terminal windows or other multiplexing will be required.

Then run:
$go run server.go
$go run client.go 1
$go run client.go 2
$go run client.go 3
$go run client.go 4
$go run client.go 5
$go run client.go 6
$go run client.go 7
$go run client.go 8

Once these are open, all nodes have a small CLI that can be used to send 
transactions to one another, mine transactions, and view the block chain as 
blocks are minted and communicated. The demo video provided demonstrates 
this functionality. 

I had a bash script that opened up these terminal windows for me and ran the
commands for testing. I have included this script, however, it is designed
specifically for my shell (Konsole from KDE Plasma), so I do not expect it to
be very portable and thus make no guarantees about its performance. However,
I figured I should still include it because it is used during the video demo
attached.
